      trivia: "Giscard d'Estaing, the brand’s instigator, was Minister of Economy and Finance at the time of its conception, but by the glittering launch of November 1974 he was already President and installed in the Élysée Palace — and the story goes that he never appeared at the debut of the state brand he had willed into being. At the presentation held in Paris for the 2017 relaunch, the founding concept of the 1970s — a cigar to accompany champagne and foie gras — was pointedly reaffirmed. That rival theories still stand as to whether the name refers to the embankment, the foreign ministry or the SEITA headquarters itself speaks of the very French reticence this marque wears."
